{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1015658-what-about-north-american-khara-i-do-not-understand-the-neanderthal-problem","id":1015658,"title":"What about North American Khara? I do not understand the \"Neanderthal\" problem.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-11T06:32:53-08:00","id":1015658,"title":"What about North American Khara? I do not understand the \"Neanderthal\" problem.","content":"OK, I'm not a werewolf expert.<br /> I love the setting, a lot, but really I do not define myself an expert.<br /> So, please, help me understand it.<br /> I do not own Shattered Dreams but, speaking with a friend of mine who has it, something struck me in recent lore about the Khara extinction.<br /> Why were Khara so concerned with (European) Neanderthal knowing their Yara while most Khara Kinfolk (maybe) inhabited North America?<br /> <br /> I mean: I know it was a problem....but it all depends on how the Khara popolation was spread and how much Khara had experience or not with Neanderthals.<br /> Neanderthals were mainly diffused in Europe.<br /> On the other hand (as far as I know) we do not have evidence about how much the Khara population was spread in the world.<br /> HOWEVER, we all know that Northern and Southern America hosted an incredible number of smilodons and related species (all possible Khara kinfolk): so I guess there was a huge population of Khara which had nothing to fear from Neanderthals (which were confined to Europe).<br /> <br /> So, is my line of reasoning wrong?<br /> Do I miss any detail? Please, help me understand it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T12:19:14-08:00","id":1015768,"title":"","content":"The Neanderthal problem was only a 'problem' for the European Khara. And wasn't even so much a 'Neanderthal' problem so much as a Garou problem. The werewolves used their advantage (the Khara Yava) to exterminate the European Khara in fairly short order. Admittedly they may not have done this (or done this so fast) had the Khara not gone around killing Neanderthal tribes (including Garou Kinfolk) and generally being asses to stop the spread of their bizarre, hitherto unknown, debilitating weakness.<br /> <br /> Khara lasted in the Americans for a bit longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}